  "description": "Scalp EEG and stereo-EEG (SEEG) recordings from 13 patients undergoing continuous video-EEG monitoring in the Penn Level 4 Epilepsy Monitoring Unit. The recordings were collected while a conversational AI agent on the patient's smartphone was linked to seizure detection that was retrained with patient and clinician feedback. Eleven patients had scalp EEG and two had SEEG. The dataset provides one EDF per recording day (69 recordings), event annotations (seizures, patient push-button events, sleep, medications, platform annotations), and derived model outputs.",
  "methods_description": "Continuous inpatient video-EEG monitoring. Scalp EEG was recorded at 256 Hz with 46 channels, and SEEG at 1024 Hz. Processing used a 0.5-100 Hz bandpass for scalp EEG and 0.5-250 Hz for intracranial EEG, with 60 and 120 Hz notch filters and common average or bipolar re-referencing depending on the algorithm. Annotations came from clinical seizure labels, patient push-button events, and a human-AI smartphone platform. EDF headers were scrubbed of dates, and the data records were left unchanged.",
